Z||000000||hugh||07-05-2000||09:51 PM||||Will the seat belts from a 1984 fit a 1988?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||07-06-2000||09:27 AM||||Ought to.  Pretty sure they're all the same.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||07-06-2000||04:02 PM||||While on the subject. Does anyone have any recommendation for cleaning seat belts? My driver side belt is getting ugly. I was thinking of taking it out and putting it in the dishwasher. Would this harm the material? I seem to remember reading that it would.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||07-06-2000||05:05 PM||||I've had pretty good luck using laundry detergent to clean up scummy seat belts.  Imagine that - using laundry detergent on fabrics?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Mixed up some powdered laundry detergent (think it was Arm & Hammer brand) in some warm water in a bucket.  Scrubbed it on with a stiff nylon bristle brush.  Rinsed off with warm water & let dry.<P> When I did it, I had the seat belts and retractors out of the car for another project.  Pulled the belts out of the retractors as far as they would go, put a clamp on them so they wouldn't wind back in.  Left the metal clips and retractor mechanism out of the bucket, and let the belts hang in the bucket of soapy water for a few hours. <BR>Next, used the scrub brush on them.  Rinsed with clean warm water, hosed them off, then let hang in air to dry.<P>Took all day, but the belts were out for other reasons, and they really gleamed when it came time to put them back in the car.  Hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !         ||||reg||6
Z||000004||Gokart||07-06-2000||08:42 PM||||Seat belts are interchangable, but most times you have to change the part the clip goes into as well. Took the ones out of my 86 2m4 parts car into the 87GT and found out later when the clip wouldn't go in that I had to swap the other piece too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||2
Z||000005||tgowens||07-06-2000||08:51 PM||||I cleaned mine with that spray on foam carpet cleaner -- worked like a charm -- I also used Goo-Gone on the seat belt guide to clean off all of the built up dirt and grime (made the interior smell good too!)||||reg||1
Z||000006||jeffozz||07-07-2000||12:46 AM||||Mr. Clean works GREAT!||||reg||1
Z||000007||webbee||07-07-2000||02:31 PM||||My current fave cleaner is Orange by Zep available from Home Depot. I buy the Gal and use it 50/50 with h2o, or straight. You have to rinse it with h2o. It rules!!!||||reg||10
Z||000008||Standard||07-07-2000||06:15 PM||||Zep Orange is the greastest cleaner known to mankind....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
